.TH SPELUNK\-SETUP 1 "" "spelunk" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
spelunk\-setup \- prepare your account for the spelunk launcher plugin
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B spelunk\-setup
[\fB\-\-no\-autostart\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-indexer\fR] [\fB\-\-help\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B spelunk\-setup
is a one\-time, per\-user setup for spelunk, which adds an "in: <words>" full\-text search to the
Super\-key launcher on Pop!_OS with COSMIC.
Run it as your normal user, never as root.
.PP
It installs a Recoll configuration, but only when you have no Recoll settings yet: an existing
configuration is never overwritten.
It makes \fI~/.recoll\fR private to your user, enables the real\-time indexer at login and starts it.
.PP
When an existing Recoll configuration does not exclude hidden files and directories, it warns you,
because their text, which can include keys and tokens, would appear in launcher results.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-no\-autostart
Do not start the indexer with your desktop session.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-indexer
Do not start the indexer now.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show a short help text.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.recoll/recoll.conf
The Recoll configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.config/autostart/recollindex.desktop
The autostart entry for the real\-time indexer.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/spelunk/indexer.log
Output of the indexer started by spelunk\-setup.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR recoll (1),
.BR recollindex (1)
.PP
The Security section of
.I /usr/share/doc/spelunk/PREREQUISITES.md
